            <ArticleTitle>Exercise management.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>13-5, 17-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Aerobic exercise is receiving increasing emphasis as an important health promoting behavior. This paper provides a model for assessment and management of the healthy exercising adult. A data base is presented that enables the practitioner to determine the presence of risk factors and/or disease, to identify health problems which might modify exercise prescription and to collect information to individualize the prescription. The remainder of the paper details the elements of exercise prescription with a specific focus on patient education.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
